  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Chindon-ya are costumed street bands hired to advertise shop openings and sales, a trade that grew in Osaka and Tokyo from the Meiji era and drew on the jinta street brass bands of the Meiji and Taishō eras. The chindon player wears a rig of a small gong and two small drums, joined by a bass drum (gorosu) and a melody player on clarinet or saxophone; the kane card stands in for the gong and the shime-daiko card for the small drums.",
